## SCORING CRITERIA

### Backend Engineering — 後端工程與 API 架構 (0-25 points)
Non-negotiable: strong programming in at least one of Python, Node.js, Go or Java; RESTful or GraphQL API design; system integration and microservices.
**HIGH (19-25):** Designed and owned production backend services or APIs at meaningful scale (high availability / high concurrency), microservice architecture, data services consumed by front ends or other teams
**MEDIUM (10-18):** Solid production backend work in one of the languages; built and maintained APIs, but limited scale or ownership
**LOW (3-9):** Mostly coursework, tutorials or minor contributions; APIs only consumed, not designed
**VERY LOW (0-2):** No backend evidence

### Data Engineering — 數據工程 (0-20 points)
Non-negotiable: proficient SQL and at least one big-data framework or tool (Spark, Kafka, Airflow, Flink, Hive, etc.); independently cleaning and refining complex data.
**HIGH (15-20):** Built production data pipelines (batch or streaming) with these tools; turned behaviour/transaction/profile data into features, services or reports used by the business
**MEDIUM (8-14):** Regular SQL and ETL work, some exposure to big-data tools in production
**LOW (2-7):** SQL only, or big-data tools only in study projects
**VERY LOW (0-1):** No data engineering evidence

### AI/LLM Application & Guardrails — AI/LLM 應用與安全護欄 (0-25 points)
Non-negotiable: generative AI / LLM development and API wrapping; hands-on AI guardrails (compliance, content safety, output validation); MLOps basics and model performance tuning.
**HIGH (19-25):** Shipped LLM or ML features to production users, including guardrails or output validation, deployment/monitoring (MLOps), and evidence of tuning cost, latency or quality
**MEDIUM (10-18):** Integrated LLM APIs or deployed ML models in real products, but little evidence of guardrails, evaluation or operations
**LOW (3-9):** Prototypes, demos, courses or hackathon-level AI work only
**VERY LOW (0-2):** No AI/LLM application evidence

### Growth & Business Impact — 商業變現與增長成果 (0-20 points)
The team is measured by delivery speed and revenue conversion; the role expects a growth-hacker mindset that ties technical work to ROI.
**HIGH (15-20):** Quantified business outcomes the candidate's work drove (revenue, conversion, retention, user growth, cost savings), recommendation or ads systems, A/B testing, fast MVP delivery
**MEDIUM (8-14):** Clear business context and plausible impact, but few or unclear numbers
**LOW (2-7):** Purely technical descriptions with no link to users or business results
**VERY LOW (0-1):** No evidence

### Relevant Experience & Collaboration — 相關年資與協作 (0-10 points)
The role asks for 3-5+ years in backend, data engineering, AI application or ML engineering.
**HIGH (8-10):** 3+ years of directly relevant experience, cross-team work (product, BI, front end, ops, sales/marketing), and use of AI-assisted development tools (Copilot, ChatGPT, etc.) in the workflow
**MEDIUM (4-7):** 1-3 years of relevant experience, or more years in adjacent areas
**LOW (0-3):** Under 1 year, internships only, or unrelated experience

